---
const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'How accurate is the jump height?',
    a: 'AIRLOG is in early beta and height accuracy is still being validated against tape-measured drops and video. We don’t publish accuracy numbers until they’re earned. Every release is checked against tape and video.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What does AIRLOG record?',
    a: 'The watch app records your session’s GPS and raw motion sensor data. After the session AIRLOG detects each jump and works out height, airtime and distance.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Which watches are supported?',
    a: 'The beta runs on the Garmin Forerunner 265 today. Venu 3, Venu 4 and the fenix 7 family are coming to the beta. The beta app is a Connect IQ app called AIRLOG Lab.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do sessions get from the watch to AIRLOG?',
    a: 'Automatic sync from the watch to AIRLOG is not built yet. It is coming. Email us with the “Join the beta” button and we’ll tell you how the beta works today.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Does it work with Strava?',
    a: 'Not yet. The Strava connection is not built yet and is coming. The plan: connect with one tap, and AIRLOG adds a short block to each activity description with your highest jump, jump count, average speed while moving, and a link to your AIRLOG session or profile. The phone on this page is a preview of that, with demo data.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Who can see my sessions?',
    a: 'Spots are public, exact tracks are private by default, and the start and end of every track are trimmed. The full details are in the privacy policy.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do I join the beta?',
    a: 'Email us with the “Join the beta” button and tell us which watch you ride with. We’ll get back to you with the details.',
  },
];
---

<section class="section" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
  <div class="wrap faq-grid">
    <header class="section-head left" data-reveal>
      <p class="eyebrow"><span class="pulse"></span>FAQ</p>
      <h2 id="faq-title">Questions, <span class="grad">answered.</span></h2>
      <p class="sub">Short answers about an early beta. We’ll add the rest as it ships.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="faq-list" data-stagger="1">
      {
        faqs.map((f, i) => (
          <details class="faq-item" name="faq" data-reveal open={i === 0}>
            <summary>
              <span>{f.q}</span>
              <i aria-hidden="true"></i>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-a"><p>{f.a}</p></div>
          </details>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
